// Rasgueado Patterns — original exercise written for OpenTabz (AGPL-3.0-or-later).
// Playback fixture: every rasgueado pattern, one beat each, over E, Am, Dm and E7.
\title "Rasgueado Patterns"
\subtitle "OpenTabz playback fixture"
\tempo 80
\track ("Flamenco Guitar" "Gtr.") {instrument acousticGuitarNylon}
\staff {score tabs}
\tuning (E4 B3 G3 D3 A2 E2)
\ts (3 4)
:4 (0.1 0.2 1.3 2.4 2.5 0.6){rasg ii} (0.1 0.2 1.3 2.4 2.5 0.6){rasg mi} (0.1 0.2 1.3 2.4 2.5 0.6){rasg miiTriplet} |
:4 (0.1 1.2 2.3 2.4 0.5){rasg miiAnapaest} (0.1 1.2 2.3 2.4 0.5){rasg pmpTriplet} (0.1 1.2 2.3 2.4 0.5){rasg pmpAnapaest} |
:4 (1.1 3.2 2.3 0.4){rasg peiTriplet} (1.1 3.2 2.3 0.4){rasg peiAnapaest} (1.1 3.2 2.3 0.4){rasg paiTriplet} |
:4 (0.1 1.2 2.3 2.4 0.5){rasg paiAnapaest} (0.1 1.2 2.3 2.4 0.5){rasg amiTriplet} (0.1 1.2 2.3 2.4 0.5){rasg amiAnapaest} |
:4 (0.1 3.2 1.3 0.4 2.5 0.6){rasg ppp} (0.1 3.2 1.3 0.4 2.5 0.6){rasg amii} (0.1 3.2 1.3 0.4 2.5 0.6){rasg amip} |
:4 (0.1 0.2 1.3 2.4 2.5 0.6){rasg eami} (0.1 0.2 1.3 2.4 2.5 0.6){rasg eamii} (0.1 0.2 1.3 2.4 2.5 0.6){rasg peami} |
(0.1 0.2 1.3 2.4 2.5 0.6).2{d}
